# tests/pins/k0.sha256 -- sha256 of K0 as hex0-seed assembles kernel/k0/k0.hex0
# (1,435 bytes).  kernel/k0/check.sh compares.  When a change to k0.asm is
# meant to alter it, update this line in the same commit and say why.
#   1,313 bytes, 40da2915...: K0 before the hex0 hand-off.
#   1,435 bytes: call 248 writes a file to the IDE disk by PIO (boot 1 of
#   tests/tinycc/hex0-handoff-check.sh writes builder-hex0's disk with it),
#   and execve zeroes the new stack's 8 MiB, as Linux's fresh pages are, so
#   a program reading stack it never wrote (tcc -g's getcwd buffer) sees
#   what it sees on Linux.
fb2093a323c60bd43c57c281c75e71ddb8870a0f67c767dc006619c77fada165  k0.bin
